Subject: [PATCH 167/207] dsv41 runner trace: STATED reads gcd named in prose

The replies name a gcd in prose ("We need gcd of A=123456789012345,
B=987654321012345.", "gcd of A=... and B=...", "the greatest common
divisor of X and Y"), and STATED only read the gcd(x, y) call. gcdOf
reads `gcd of` / `greatest common divisor of` over two literal decimal
integers (thousands commas, each maybe after an inline `Name=`) joined
by `and` or `, `, then a sentence end, as the same gcd statement.

Names, expressions, hex, decimals, negatives, zero-led literals, a third
number, a comma-split of grouped literals ("12,345, 18"), a claim or a
doubt refuse.

(cherry picked from commit b6edf01a9815465252ec3df25450f2d0cc277b3e)
